questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where an order processing system encounters `org.springframework.transaction.UnexpectedRollbackException` in logs. When inventory reservation fails, the service catches the custom `RuntimeException` to write a failure audit record to the database within the same request flow, but the entire transaction rolls back and the audit log is lost.

java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired
    private InventoryService inventoryService;
    @Autowired
    private AuditRepository auditRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processOrder(Order order) {
        try {
            inventoryService.reserveItems(order);
        } catch (InventoryException e) {
            // Attempt to log audit record in database upon failure
            auditRepository.save(new AuditLog(order.getId(), "INVENTORY_FAILED"));
        }
    }
}

@Service
public class InventoryService {
    @Transactional
    public void reserveItems(Order order) {
        if (order.isOutOfStock()) {
            throw new InventoryException("Item out of stock"); // Extends RuntimeException
        }
    }
}
